nllm_bitfield_compressor-0.1.0.dist-info/WHEEL,sha256=DYTgwV0XsDRc_ZG5tOWurK6Fa3sZsRK-qV8xaC2kLYI,105\nllm_bitfield_compressor-0.1.0.dist-info/direct_url.json,sha256=tgiCNFJOBH7tZwx4b1P-rKbhxDYZn6P39r6fx11ScpU,84\nllm_bitfield_compressor-0.1.0.dist-info/top_level.txt,sha256=2oYlr17akxVbT2tsU9cskYmHIeyQNd0G_nKbqhBrS4o,59\nllm_bitfield_compressor-0.1.0.dist-info/uv_build.json,sha256=RBNvo1WzZ4oRRq0W9-hknpT7T8If536DEMBg9hyq_4o,2\nllm_bitfield_compressor-0.1.0.dist-info/uv_cache.json,sha256=ASHq0JE4d3O7CcUXGz3GKLl8jVkRxXE75tUWPRBmNrU,137\n/root/projects/tiered-serve/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/llm_bitfield_compressor-0.1.0.dist-info/METADATA\n--- /root/projects/tiered-serve/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/llm_bitfield_compressor-0.1.0.dist-info/METADATA\nMetadata-Version: 2.4\nName: LLM-bitfield-compressor\nVersion: 0.1.0\nSummary: Splits BF16 floating-point weights into sign, exponent (8-bit), and mantissa (7-bit) bit-fields, then benchmarks compression across CPU and GPU algorithms.\nRequires-Python: >=3.12\nDescription-Content-Type: text/markdown\nRequires-Dist: cmake==3.*\nRequires-Dist: numpy\nRequires-Dist: torch\nRequires-Dist: safetensors\nRequires-Dist: huggingface_hub\nRequires-Dist: transformers\nRequires-Dist: nvidia-nvcomp-cu13\nRequires-Dist: zstandard\nRequires-Dist: lz4\n\n# LLM Bitfield Compressor — DEPRECATED\n\n> **This repository is deprecated.**\n>\n> The source of truth for ZipServ / DietGPU / P4-flat / P4-D16 /\n> P3-flat-FP8 / DietGPU-FP8 codec implementations has moved into\n> [tiered-serve](https://github.com/Sys-KU/TieredServe) under\n> `tiered_serve/compression/`.  Selected ablation variants from this\n> repo (FP8-ANS, FP8 e3-split, P4 variants ablation, DietGPU\n> two-stream-fused MM, pybridge reference) were copied into\n> `tiered-serve/experimental/codec_variants/` as part of the\n> compression-subsystem migration.\n>\n> This repo is kept read-only for history and external paper-artifact\n> references.  Do not start new work here.\n\n---\n\nBF16 LLM weight compression benchmark suite. Splits BF16 floating-point weights into sign, exponent (8-bit), and mantissa (7-bit) bit-fields, then benchmarks compression across CPU and GPU algorithms.\n\n---\n\n## Scripts\n\nAll runnable scripts live in `scripts/`. Run them from the project root:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python scripts/<script>.py <args>\n```\n\n### scripts/compress_weights.py\n\n**Weight compression benchmark.** Splits BF16 weights into exponent (8-bit) and mantissa (7-bit) fields, compresses each with ZipServ-TBE, nvCOMP (ANS/Bitcomp), DietGPU (Float/ANS), FPcompress (CPU/GPU), and CPU baselines (zlib/lz4/zstd). Reports Full/Exp/Mant compression ratios, latency (ms), and throughput (GB/s). Supports `--tile` for per-tile zstd with 2D tile reordering.\n\n```bash\n# Basic: benchmark all projection weights in a shard\n.venv/bin/python scripts/compress_weights.py model-00001-of-00030.safetensors\n\n# Limit to first N weights\n.venv/bin/python scripts/compress_weights.py model-00001-of-00030.safetensors --max-weights 3\n\n# Include non-projection weights (embed, norm, etc.)\n.venv/bin/python scripts/compress_weights.py model-00001-of-00030.safetensors --all-weights\n\n# Per-tile zstd compression with specific tile sizes\n.venv/bin/python scripts/compress_weights.py model-00001-of-00030.safetensors --tile 64 256 1024\n\n# Save compressed outputs for later inspection\n.venv/bin/python scripts/compress_weights.py model-00001-of-00030.safetensors \\\n    --extract compressed_out\n\n# Multiple timing runs for stable latency numbers\n.venv/bin/python scripts/compress_weights.py model-00001-of-00030.safetensors --runs 5\n```\n\n| Argument | Type | Default | Description |\n|----------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `shard` | positional | *(required)* | Path to `.safetensors` shard file |\n| `--all-weights` | flag | off | Include all weights, not just projections |\n| `--runs` | int | 3 | Number of compress/decompress timing runs (median-based) |\n| `--max-weights` | int | 0 (all) | Max number of weights to benchmark |\n| `--extract DIR` | str | None | Save compressed data to `DIR/<tensor>/<compressor>.pt` |\n| `--tile N [N ...]` | int list | None | Enable per-tile zstd with given tile sizes (64, 256, 1024 recommended) |\n\n### scripts/reconstruct_weights.py\n\n**Reconstruction benchmark.** Measures BF16 reconstruction and decompress latency across paths for 7 Llama-class projection layers. JIT-compiles `cuda/reconstruct_cuda.cu` on first run.\n\nOutput columns per (layer, GEMM-N) row:\n\n| Column | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| `GEMM` | cuBLAS BF16 GEMM only |\n| `Reconstruction` | CUDA reconstruct kernel (exp+sm → BF16) |\n| `Decomp(Zipserv)` | ZipServ GPU TCA-TBE decompression |\n| `Decomp(DietGPU)` | DietGPU ANS decode to exp buffer |\n| `Fusing(Decomp+Reconstruct,DietGPU)` | DietGPU single-kernel fused ANS+reconstruct |\n| `SUM(Zipserv)` | `Decomp(Zipserv)` + `GEMM` |\n| `SUM(DietGPU)` | `Reconstruction` + `Decomp(DietGPU)` + `GEMM` |\n| `D+R->G(DietGPU)` | `Fusing(Decomp+Reconstruct)` + `GEMM` (sequential, default stream) |\n\n```bash\n# Full layer sweep (all layers: Q, K, V, O, Gate, Up, Down)\n.venv/bin/python scripts/reconstruct_weights.py\n\n# Specific layers and shorter timing loop\n.venv/bin/python scripts/reconstruct_weights.py --layers Q K V Gate Up --warmup 3 --runs 10\n\n# GEMM N sweep for a single layer\n.venv/bin/python scripts/reconstruct_weights.py --layers O --gemm-ns 1 2 4 8 16 32 64 128 --warmup 5 --runs 20\n```\n\n| Argument | Type | Default | Description |\n|----------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `--layers` | str list | `Q K V O Gate Up Down` | Layer names to benchmark |\n| `--gemm-ns` | int list | `16 32 64 128 256 512 1024 2048 4096 8192` | GEMM N sweep (token batch sizes) |\n| `--warmup` | int | 5 | Warmup iterations |\n| `--runs` | int | 20 | Timed iterations |\n\n### scripts/compress_mantissa_tiles.py\n\n**Per-tile mantissa compression benchmark.** Focuses on mantissa-only compression across tile sizes 16×16 to 1024×1024. Compares ZipServ-TBE, all nvCOMP algorithms (8 variants), DietGPU ANS, zstd, and Shannon entropy lower bound. Includes decompression throughput (GB/s) measurement. Each NxN tile is compressed independently.\n\n```bash\n# Benchmark all projection weights\n.venv/bin/python scripts/compress_mantissa_tiles.py model-00001-of-00030.safetensors\n\n# Include all weight types\n.venv/bin/python scripts/compress_mantissa_tiles.py model-00001-of-00030.safetensors --all-weights\n\n# Filter to a specific layer\n.venv/bin/python scripts/compress_mantissa_tiles.py model-00001-of-00030.safetensors --layer 0\n\n# Limit number of weights\n.venv/bin/python scripts/compress_mantissa_tiles.py model-00001-of-00030.safetensors --max-weights 2\n```\n\n| Argument | Type | Default | Description |\n|----------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `shard` | positional | *(required)* | Path to `.safetensors` shard file |\n| `--all-weights` | flag | off | Include all weights, not just projections |\n| `--max-weights` | int | 0 (all) | Max number of weights to process |\n| `--layer` | str | None | Filter by layer number (substring match) |\n\n### scripts/analyze_bitfields.py\n\n**Bit-field analysis tool.** Inspects sign/exponent/mantissa bit-field distributions, per-field entropy, value statistics, exponent and mantissa histograms, per-row/column entropy variation. Supports `--key` to select a specific tensor and `--as-bf16` to reinterpret data.\n\n```bash\n# Analyze all projection weights in a shard\n.venv/bin/python scripts/analyze_bitfields.py model-00001-of-00030.safetensors\n\n# Analyze a specific tensor by key\n.venv/bin/python scripts/analyze_bitfields.py model-00001-of-00030.safetensors \\\n    --key model.layers.0.mlp.down_proj.weight\n\n# Filter by layer number\n.venv/bin/python scripts/analyze_bitfields.py model-00001-of-00030.safetensors --layer 0\n\n# Show top 20 exponent/mantissa values\n.venv/bin/python scripts/analyze_bitfields.py model-00001-of-00030.safetensors --top 20\n\n# Reinterpret raw bytes as BF16\n.venv/bin/python scripts/analyze_bitfields.py model-00001-of-00030.safetensors --as-bf16\n/root/projects/tiered-serve/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/llm_bitfield_compressor-0.1.0.dist-info/WHEEL\n--- /root/projects/tiered-serve/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/llm_bitfield_compressor-0.1.0.dist-info/WHEEL\nWheel-Version: 1.0\nGenerator: setuptools (79.0.1)\nRoot-Is-Purelib: false\nTag: cp312-cp312-linux_aarch64\n\n/root/projects/tiered-serve/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/llm_bitfield_compressor-0.1.0.dist-info/INSTALLER\n--- /root/projects/tiered-serve/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/llm_bitfield_compressor-0.1.0.dist-info/INSTALLER\nuv/root/projects/tiered-serve/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/llm_bitfield_compressor-0.1.0.dist-info/REQUESTED\n--- /root/projects/tiered-serve/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/llm_bitfield_compressor-0.1.0.dist-info/REQUESTED\n/root/projects/tiered-serve/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/llm_bitfield_compressor-0.1.0.dist-info/uv_cache.json\n--- /root/projects/tiered-serve/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/llm_bitfield_compressor-0.1.0.dist-info/uv_cache.json\n{\"timestamp\":{\"secs_since_epoch\":1779768976,\"nanos_since_epoch\":781985544},\"commit\":null,\"tags\":null,\"env\":{},\"directories\":{\"src\":null}}/root/projects/tiered-serve/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/llm_bitfield_compressor-0.1.0.dist-info/uv_build.json\n--- /root/projects/tiered-serve/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/llm_bitfield_compressor-0.1.0.dist-info/uv_build.json\n{}/root/projects/tiered-serve/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/__pycache__/__editable___llm_bitfield_compressor_0_1_0_finder.cpython-312.pyc\n--- /root/projects/tiered-serve/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/__pycache__/__editable___llm_bitfield_compressor_0_1_0_finder.cpython-312.pyc\n�\r\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000+��iq\r\u0000\u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000